EXAMPLE TENANTS — GAME SERVER EMULATORS
================================================================================

The example tenants deploy open-source server emulators. Those projects are
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2, by their respective
authors. This repository redistributes none of their source.

This repository contains NO game data, and NO mechanism for obtaining any.

Running these emulators requires data derived from a game client. That data is
copyrighted by its publisher and is not distributed, referenced, or made
obtainable by anything in this repository. Obtaining it, and determining whether
your use is lawful in your jurisdiction and consistent with the publisher's
terms, is entirely the operator's responsibility.

The example tenants exist to demonstrate multi-tenancy on Kubernetes using
workloads whose behaviour differs instructively from a web application — raw TCP
without hostname multiplexing, per-tenant databases, and a simulation that does
not scale horizontally. They are provided for EDUCATIONAL PURPOSES.

The upstream projects themselves note that operating a public or commercial
server may be unlawful in many jurisdictions. This project takes no position
beyond theirs, asserts no more than they do, and offers no legal advice.
